Gemini CLI | gemini -p "prompt" | Yes (1000 req/day) | --output-format json, jsonl (streaming) | https://geminicli.com/docs/cli/headless/
Copilot CLI | copilot -p "prompt" --allow-tool=''shell(git)'' | Yes (2000 completion/mo) | --output-format json (JSONL) | https://docs.github.com/copilot/concepts/agents/about-copilot-cli
OpenCode | opencode run "prompt" | Yes (Zen free tier) | --format json (JSONL event stream) | https://opencode.ai/docs/cli/
Cursor | agent -p "prompt" | Yes (Hobby free tier) | --output-format stream-json, --stream-partial-output | https://cursor.com/docs/cli/headless

VERIFICATION CHECKLIST:
- 5 tool rows: Goose, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI, OpenCode, Cursor [OK]
- Each row has headless command example [OK]
- Each row has free/paid account requirement with conditions [OK]
- Each row has stream-JSON/JSONL output format flag [OK]
- Each row has official documentation source URL [OK - 5 sources]

EVALUATION AND RECOMMENDATIONS:

Top 3 Recommended Tools: Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI, OpenCode

Gemini CLI recommended as first motor-adapter. Reason: Direct access to Google''s official Gemini API; free tier provides 1000 requests/day suitable for light to medium automation; full streaming support via --output-format jsonl; reliable headless execution with simple -p flag. Sources: official GitHub repo and geminicli.com documentation.

Copilot CLI as second choice. Reason: Strong GitHub ecosystem integration; free tier offers 2000 completions/month for light automation tasks; JSONL support via --output-format json; risk: heavy usage incurs significant credit costs. Sources: docs.github.com/copilot and pricing documentation.

OpenCode as third choice. Reason: Lightweight Go-based architecture; raw event streaming via --format json (JSONL); ideal for CI/CD pipeline automation; concern: OpenCode Zen requires API key and has limited documentation for setup cost. Sources: opencode.ai/docs/cli/

RESEARCH METHODOLOGY:
- WebSearch used to investigate each tool''s headless mode, pricing, output formats
- WebFetch used to verify official documentation (GitHub repos, official sites)
- 5 official source URLs validated through direct documentation review
- Verified information only - no assumptions or guesses','cinar','2026-09-19T01:44:28+00:00');
